    "id": "01a00d54-9ab6-7370-acc6-a2d79bf7ea44:64",
    "text": "The spec is ready. Here's what I found and the plan:\n\n## Diagnosis\n\n**The BE is fine — this is an FE parsing bug.** I pulled the raw stored message from the daemon DB (`agent_message` row for that 9:26 AM message): the daemon stored the text verbatim and correctly. The message contains, mid-sentence, the literal inline code `` `<group:>` ``.\n\nThe FE tag scanner in `messageParser.ts` misparses it. Its \"malformed group open\" fallback matches `<group:` followed by anything up to the next newline:\n\n````typescript path=packages/cloudlands-fe/src/lib/utils/messageParser.ts mode=EXCERPT\nconst GROUP_AND_THINK_TAG_REGEX =\n  /<group:([^>\\n<]+)>|<group:([^\\n<]+)\\n|<group:([^>\\n<]+)$|.../g;\n````\n\nBecause that second alternative's name capture allows `>` and backticks, the literal `` `<group:>` `` inside inline code matched and swallowed the entire rest of the sentence as a \"group name\" — exactly what your screenshot shows: the message splits at ``...content and ` ``, and a bogus group appears whose header is `` >` tags. The implementor fixed all three in `f1770a3`... ``. The trailing `<!-- suggested-prompts -->` block then landed inside that bogus group's children, which is why it rendered raw instead of becoming chips.\n\n## Plan (one task, FE-only)\n\nThe [spec](intent://local/note/spec) has the full root cause, the verbatim repro payload for a regression test, and one task:\n\n1. **[Fix group/think tag scanning](intent://local/task/b8e42451-f9b9-475e-ac32-be070591281f)** — make `groupContentBlocks` ignore tag matches inside inline code spans and fenced code blocks, tighten the malformed-open fallback so its name capture excludes `>` (a literal `<group:>` then never opens a group), keep all documented malformed-tag recovery behaviors, and add a regression test using the exact stored message. Verify with the targeted vitest suite + `pnpm run check` + renderer tsc, then PR on intent-hq/cloudlands-fe.\n\nAfter implementation, a verifier agent reviews against the spec. I found no duplicate issue on intent-hq/monorepo; I'll file one (`component:fe`, `agent-filed`) when delegating so the PR can carry `Fixes intent-hq/monorepo#N`.\n\nPlease review and approve the plan above.\n\n<!-- suggested-prompts\nApprove the plan and delegate the fix.\nShow me the exact regex match trace on the stored message.\n-->\n"
